{"name":"San Juan","hex":"#445761","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"San Juan","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A province towards the northwest of Argentina.","A city, the capital of San Juan province, Argentina."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/San_Juan"}],"entries":[{"title":"San Juan, Puerto Rico","blocks":[{"text":"San Juan is the capital city and most populous municipality in Puerto Rico, an unincorporated territory and insular area of the United States. San Juan was founded by Spanish colonists in 1521, who called it Ciudad de Puerto Rico."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/2013_Old_San_Juan_01.JPG/330px-2013_Old_San_Juan_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Juan%2C_Puerto_Rico"},{"title":"San Juan, Argentina","blocks":[{"text":"San Juan is the capital and largest city of the Argentine province of San Juan in the Cuyo region, located in the Tulúm Valley, west of the San Juan River, at 650 m (2,133 ft) above mean sea level, with a population of around 112,000 as per the 2001 census [INDEC]."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Collage_Ciudad_de_San_Juan.jpg/330px-Collage_Ciudad_de_San_Juan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Juan%2C_Argentina"},{"title":"Juan","blocks":[{"text":"Juan is a given name, the Spanish and Manx versions of John. The name is of Hebrew origin and has the meaning \"God has been gracious.\" It is very common in Spain and in other Spanish-speaking countries around the world and in the Philippines, and also in the Isle of Man. The name is popular around the world and can be pronounced differently according the region. In Spanish, the diminutive form is Juanito, with feminine form Juana, and feminine diminutive Juanita."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juan"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/San_Juan_Puerto_Rico_%2833519972611%29.jpg/500px-San_Juan_Puerto_Rico_%2833519972611%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/San_Juan_Puerto_Rico_%2833519972611%29.jpg/1280px-San_Juan_Puerto_Rico_%2833519972611%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/San_Juan_Puerto_Rico_%2833519972611%29.jpg/500px-San_Juan_Puerto_Rico_%2833519972611%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASan_Juan_Puerto_Rico_(33519972611).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Castillo_San_Felipe_del_Morro_in_San_Juan_Puerto_Rico.jpg/500px-Castillo_San_Felipe_del_Morro_in_San_Juan_Puerto_Rico.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Castillo_San_Felipe_del_Morro_in_San_Juan_Puerto_Rico.jpg/1280px-Castillo_San_Felipe_del_Morro_in_San_Juan_Puerto_Rico.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Castillo_San_Felipe_del_Morro_in_San_Juan_Puerto_Rico.jpg/500px-Castillo_San_Felipe_del_Morro_in_San_Juan_Puerto_Rico.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACastillo_San_Felipe_del_Morro_in_San_Juan_Puerto_Rico.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Old_San_Juan_-_City_Hall.jpg/500px-Old_San_Juan_-_City_Hall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Old_San_Juan_-_City_Hall.jpg/1280px-Old_San_Juan_-_